                "text": "**Analyzing the Pattern**\n\nI'm deep in the weeds analyzing the provided training example. A vertical line of '2's and a horizontal line of '4's intersect. The intersection in the input is '4', but it changes to '2' in the output. I'm trying to determine if the '2' took precedence, or if there's some kind of continuous transformation at play. I'm going to have to make a better hypothesis.\n\n\n**Refining the Hypothesis**\n\nI've been going over example 2, and the diagonal patterns. Now I think I'm closer to an accurate model of these intersections. The interrupted line gets restored, even when it interrupts the other line. I'm starting to build a better idea of how precedence might work in different scenarios. I'm going to look at Ex 3 again with this new perspective.\n\n\n**Exploring the Weave**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on Example 3. I see a vertical '3' interrupted by a horizontal '2', and a vertical '6' interrupted by the '2'. The output shows '2's continuous and '6' continuous, but the '3' is interrupted. I'm considering an alternating weave model or perhaps a z-order. Example 4 confirms this; a continuous '7' gets interrupted by a diagonal '3' in the output. I'm looking for the underlying rule.\n\n\n",
